> Q1:
> Is it possible to change colors in the geno.image plots?
>
> First, thinking of people with colorblindness, the red/green
> combination is not ideal.
> And second, sometimes, we have colors for different parents which we
> would want to use in different types of plots for consistency. In such
> cases, it would be gread, if there would be the option to choose own
> colors for AA, AB, BB and not rely on the default red, blue, green.

You can pass the argument 'col' with a vector of colors, which will be
passed to image() which makes the actual plot.

> Q2:
> Would it be feasible, to draw the figure to map scale (instead of
> using the consecutive marker order only)? For simplicity, the
> recombination breakpoint could be drawn in the middle between two
> markers (when genotypes change from AA to AB or AA to BB).

It's feasible.

karl

